{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1452656-plothooks-in-the-early-days-of-the-order-of-reason","id":1452656,"title":"Plothooks in the early days of the order of reason","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-17T11:10:45-07:00","id":1452656,"title":"Plothooks in the early days of the order of reason","content":"I'll never play these quests, but I have a few ideas. <br /> <br /> I like steampunk. I like the craftmasons. I like medieval fantasy. So why not possible story hooks in the early days of the order of reason, when things were so odd, so incredible, and yet, things were about to change? <br /> <br /> #1. A member of the ex chequers have been going around, trying out some new fangled stuff from the crafters and planters. They say it's going to improve agricultural yields. And the exchequer? Well, he wants the cut of the extra harvest. Satisfaction guaranteed, or your money back, he says. A pinch of fast talking and the locals are interested. Sadly he's gotten into a tiff with 2 people who are rather upset. One is the verbena, who dislike the idea of anyone encroaching on their turf, and the other is the local lord, who believes that the residents having more food would give them space to rebel<br /> <br /> #2. Several Garou have been attacking a nearby logging camp. Your job is to flush them out, destroy them, and purge any nearby kinfolk nests. <br /> <br /> #3. You're a newfound mage here working for the Order of Reason. Trained in seduction, art, conversation, subterfuge, and politics, your job is to infiltrate the gaslamp and perfumed hallways of European powers... and deal with all threats, physical and political, to the Order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:45:17-07:00","id":1452661,"title":"","content":"These are all really good hooks. But doesn\u2019t number 2 in particular cast the Order in a villainous role?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:53:28-07:00","id":1452664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1452656-plothooks-in-the-early-days-of-the-order-of-reason?p=1452661#post1452661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are all really good hooks. But doesn\u2019t number 2 in particular cast the Order in a villainous role?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. <br /> <br /> Let's be frank here. <br /> <br /> Werewolves are heroes. But they're heroes compared to Pentex. Considering the many many issues, and what werewolves can be like during the time of the Order of reason... Yup. <br /> <br /> Generally a lot of supernatural baddies. Not just the common lineup, but lots of weaker ones too. Little monsters that any mage would laugh at but give normal people a run for their money. Weaker beasts that would have been exterminated in the modern age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T00:08:12-07:00","id":1452743,"title":"","content":"Also: being involved in logging doesn't automatically make you Wyrm-tainted. If it's done with care, it can in fact be healthy for the forest by removing dead trees that would otherwise become kindling for wildfires. Not that most loggers have thought that way, historically; a more likely mindset for them has been to make a living and to put food on the table for their families. <br /> <br /> The point is that it's not hard to portray the logging camp as innocent victims of werewolf aggression; and in an Order of Reason chronicle, it's appropriate to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T08:44:56-07:00","id":1453168,"title":"","content":"The lord in #1 says so much about the region, doesn't it? Presumably he has a reason for suspecting rebellion, so it's either happened before or he's a really suspicious weasel of a lord. That says a lot about his relation with his lands, what the people have experienced.<br /> <br /> Although a third option is he is another member of the OoR (or rejected member) trying out a form of political philosophy on the locals and this is messing with his plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}